## 0. Things to know before using this (conflicts and corrections found in the references)

1. **Italic emphasis font conflict.** [V] The reference sets emphasis words ("Kitchenware", "Products", "sellers", "Arrival", "Gallery", author surnames, "96%") in a high-contrast serif italic. Your mandated fonts (Bricolage Grotesque + DM Sans) have **no true italic**, so italics will be browser-synthesised obliques of Bricolage. [R] The prompt follows your two-font rule, and exposes one CSS token (`--font-accent`) so a single serif italic can be switched on later if you want closer fidelity. It is OFF by default.
2. **Leaked draft copy.** [V] The hero paragraph reads "…much like the original banner. Let me know if you'd like adjustments!" That is AI chat text left in the design, and "A OasiSteam showcases…" contains a stray "A". [R] The prompt supplies clean replacement copy.
3. **Glass card vs. "no glassmorphism".** [V] The hero "96%" card is a translucent green panel. [R] Implemented as a mostly opaque tinted panel with a very light blur, which preserves the look without a glassmorphism aesthetic.
4. **Newsletter overlap.** [V] The top-right newsletter photo overlaps the "f" of "10% Off". [R] Treated as a presentation flaw. The prompt keeps the staggered image layout but forbids text being covered.
5. **Testimonial card sizing quirk.** [V] The active (white) review card is shorter and sits lower than its cream neighbours. [R] Reproduced deliberately as an "inset active card" state, since it reads as intentional.
6. **Badge contrast.** [V] White text on translucent pills over light-grey product backgrounds is low-contrast. [R] Fixed with an ivory, mostly opaque pill and dark-green text.
7. **Brand casing.** [V] "Homedine" in the wordmark and "HomeDine" in review text. [R] Standardised to **Homedine**.
8. **Demo claims.** The "4.9/5", "25,000+ reviews", "96%", the reviewer names and the prices are placeholder content. [R] Labelled as demo data in code. Don't publish unverified rating or sustainability claims.
9. **Exact values are not measurable.** All hex values and pixel sizes below are approximations from scaled screenshots, not source values.
10. **Section list vs. actual page.** Your suggested 15-item order merges into 13 real sections (see §2).

